       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day. That is twice the labeled maximum for adults of 3,200 mg/day. A single 1,600 mg dose is also double the usual maximum single dose of 800 mg. At this level the risks of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events go up a lot, and the extra dose adds no analgesic benefit.\n\nHere are some options within labeled limits:\n- **Ibuprofen 800 mg PO four times daily (3,200 mg/day).** This is the maximum for anti-inflammatory use.\n- **Ibuprofen 600 mg PO four times daily (2,400 mg/day).** This is a common dose for pain or inflammation.\n- **Ibuprofen 400 mg PO every 4\u20136 hours as needed.** This is for mild to moderate pain.\n\nIf you meant 1600 mg per day, for example 400 mg four times daily, I can enter that. If the patient needs more analgesia than these doses give, you could add acetaminophen or consider another approach.\n\nTell me which dose and frequency you want, and I'll enter it."
